//  Out-of-combat healing. Both hands are offered a turn: on our two-handed
//  staves the healing ability is the primary item's altAbility, not anything in
//  the alt slot, and nicemice_resolveAbilityIntent resolves that.
//
//  A selector, not a parallel -- only one hand may own the aim per tick.
//
//  DRAWING FIRST. Nothing outside combat unsheathes for an NPC, so a medic that
//  has never been in a fight is holding nothing: self.primary is empty, the
//  staff is sitting in sheathedprimary, and every nicemice_resolveAbilityIntent
//  below fails on "ability: none". That is why medics walked past bleeding
//  allies until something shot at them.
//
//  The draw is gated on all three of: nothing usable already in hand, a staff
//  actually stowed, and that stowed staff resolving a healing intent (which is
//  what nicemice_resolveAbilityIntent's sheathed flag is for -- it reads the
//  stowed slots instead of the held ones). Only then do we pay for the ally scan
//  that decides whether anybody needs it. A succeeder wraps the whole thing so
//  an NPC that already has its staff out drops straight through to the cast.
//
//  Nothing here re-sheathes afterwards, matching combat: vanilla leaves NPCs
//  armed once they draw, and racing the combat tree for the item slots would
//  only cost us casts.
//
//  nicemice_chargedFire reads the item's charge stance, holds for its duration
//  and then releases once. NPCs have no input release edge of their own, and
//  without one the ability sits in charged{} forever and never discharges.
//
//  Effect zones are placed at the aim point and never steer, so entityInRange
//  gates on the real radial distance rather than casting short of the ally.
//
//  requireLineOfSight: turn off in walled test arenas where allies sit behind
//  pillars. debugTargeting: log every ally candidate and filter result.
{
  "name": "nicemice_healsupport",
  "description": "",
  "scripts": [
    "/scripts/behavior.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/nicemice_wandstaff.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/npc.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/movement.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/entity.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/time.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/position.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/world.lua",
    "/scripts/actions/nicemice_whipaim.lua"
  ],
  "parameters": {
    "healRange": 20,
    "idleHealCooldown": 3,
    "castRangeMargin": 5,
    "requireLineOfSight": true,
    "debugTargeting": false,
    "castRangeFallback": 25
  },
